---
// Footer.astro
---

<footer class="site-footer glass">
  <div class="container footer-content">
    <div class="footer-meta">
      <div class="footer-logo">
        <span class="f-logo-icon">🇪🇺</span>
        <span class="f-logo-text">PhD<span class="highlight">Europe</span></span>
      </div>
      <p class="footer-desc">A side project that puts PhD pay, living costs, tuition and visa rules side by side, so picking where to spend the next three or four years is a little less of a guessing game.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="footer-sources">
      <h2 class="sources-title">About the Data</h2>
      <ul class="sources-list">
        <li>Pay comes from official pay tables and funder rules, cited on every country page. Tax and contribution rates come from the OECD, price levels from Eurostat, life satisfaction from the World Happiness Report.</li>
        <li>Living costs, tuition and some programme details are still the author's estimates, and the site labels them as such. <a href={`https://github.com/kazulak/find-country-for-phd/blob/main/docs/DATA_SOURCES.md`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">How the data is built</a>.</li>
        <li>This is a snapshot, not an official source. Always confirm with the university or funder. Found a wrong number? <a href="https://github.com/kazulak/find-country-for-phd/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open an issue</a>.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="footer-bottom">
    <div class="container bottom-container">
      <span class="copyright">© 2026 <a href="https://github.com/kazulak" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@kazulak</a> · <a href="https://github.com/kazulak/find-country-for-phd" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Source on GitHub</a> · MIT License</span>
      <span class="credit">Built with heavy AI assistance (Claude Code) · Astro, React and plain YAML.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>

<style>
  .site-footer {
    margin: 40px 24px 24px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 40px 0 0;
    margin-top: auto; /* Push to bottom */
  }
  
  .footer-content {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 40px;
    padding-bottom: 40px;
  }
  
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .footer-content {
      grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 1.8fr;
      gap: 60px;
    }
  }
  
  .footer-meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  
  .footer-logo {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  
  .f-logo-icon {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
  }
  
  .highlight {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--primary), var(--secondary));
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
  }
  
  .footer-desc {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  
  .footer-sources {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  
  .sources-title {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  
  .sources-list {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  
  .sources-list li {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 14px;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  
  .sources-list li::before {
    content: "▪";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--primary-hover);
  }
  
  .footer-bottom {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    padding: 20px 0;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
  }
  
  .bottom-container {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  
  .copyright {
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  
  .credit {
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .site-footer a {
    color: var(--primary-hover);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
